# OPERATIONS §2.3 (M3): check does everything load does, its last check included: a literal key at a literal stepped
# range, which load refuses wherever it is written, a def no ask reads included (L §2.5, §8.4; tally 2.1.7 R5, #106).
# The text of L8_4_load_sees_literal_key: the base's one refusal line, as run prints it, exit 1.
=== options check exit=1
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input r[d in 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 step 7 days]: int

def w: int = r[2026-01-09]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r[*] = 0 "s"

ask q: r[2026-01-15]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY 2026-01-09 is not a value of 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 step 7 day ...
